From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Project Luma <engineering@projectluma.org>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 03:00:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Luma Connect Sync: approval card, status cell and restoring
 tiles
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Reads org.projectluma.ConnectSync1 (luma-connect-sync, ADR-054).

Approval card: when a device asks to join (ListJoinRequests on start,
JoinRequested), every member shows a Shell-owned card at the top centre
above windows: "LUMA CONNECT", the device's class glyph, "Approve
ThinkPad?", one sentence, the six digits in two wells, and Not me and
Approve at equal width. Approve calls ApproveJoin(join, code), Not me
DenyJoin. The card stays until the request leaves ListJoinRequests
(answered here or on another device; JoinCleared, and a 20 s re-read while
a card is up); nothing times out. One card at a time, oldest first. Phone:
a bottom sheet with 44 px buttons; TV: x1.5 with the focus on Not me.

Status cell: one of the island's status slots (QuickSettings.setStatusCell,
its own button) only for syncing (refresh-cw), paused (cloud-off) or
attention (cloud-alert amber; cloud-off red when removed). A click opens
a 312 px shell pop: "Luma Connect", the state's tile, title and line, the
progress bar while syncing, one sentence and at most one action (Sync now,
Show versions, Manage storage, Sign in again), and Sync settings (Settings
launch-panel ('users', ['sync']); Show versions ['sync', 'versions', APP];
Sign in again opens Luma Connect's sign-in). Phone: the
cell in the status bar's right group, the pop a bottom drawer
(status.html ?posture=phone: grab handle, 44 px tile, the action and Sync
settings as 44 px buttons side by side);
TV: the top bar's status group and a sheet at TV scale at the top right (the
TV quick panel has no page model). Storage full and Removed from Sync post
one banner each from "Luma Connect"; conflicts never do. A device that joins
with the recovery key (RecoveryJoined) posts one banner on every syncing
device, "ThinkPad joined with your recovery key", with Remove… (Settings
['sync', 'remove', DEVICE]) and It was me; it stays until answered. On a TV
these notices are the shared TV toast (the TV code routes every banner
there); the recovery-key one says "Not you? Remove it from the quick panel.",
where its actions are. A TV notice that informs goes through the toast,
with its actions in the quick panel; one that asks for a decision is an
offer card (0383).

Re-review B3/S1/B2 (design-center f10cf9b): a card comes as soon as this
device answers a join, before its code exists ("··· ···", a turning loader,
"Waiting for its code"; Approve waits, Not me works) and becomes the
approval card in place when the code arrives (ListJoinRequests every 2 s
meanwhile); held requests get no card. A replaced recovery key
(attention new_recovery_key) shows a warn cell; its popover says "Your old
words stopped working" and Show new key… opens Settings ('users', ['sync',
'newkey']).

Restoring apps (GetRestore, RestoreChanged): an app's grid, dock and launcher
drawer tile (lumaPresentation/appDrawer.js, in luma-shell-presentation) at
55% opacity and saturation 0.5 with a 3 px accent ring and "Restoring…";
activating it runs `luma-installer --restore APP` instead of the app.
Valet is opened once when restore rows first appear.

Glyphs: Lucide cloud, cloud-off, cloud-alert, refresh-cw, laptop,
smartphone and tv as luma-sync-*-symbolic in the Shell's icon resource.
Copy and states: lumaConnectSyncModel.js (no gi imports; checked in %check
by connect-sync-policy.js).

Design: design-center 38858a5, mockups/connect-sync (approve.html,
status.html, restore.html; cs.css, cs.js).
